    "### Ideal Dataset(s):\n",
    "\n",
    "We plan to analyze a numerical dataset spanning roughly the past 10 years, including daily observations of Bitcoin prices (BP), the S&P 500 Index (SP500), gold prices (GP), and the U.S. Dollar Index (USDI), yielding approximately 3,000 date-indexed observations. To evaluate the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on correlations or predictive relationships between Bitcoin and these financial indicators, we will incorporate a pandemic-related variable. This may be represented either as a categorical predictor indicating whether each observation falls before, during, or after the pandemic period (derivable from dates), or as a continuous variable called PandemicSeverity, ranging from 0 to 1. In this formulation, 0 represents no pandemic impact (pre-COVID), while values greater than 0 indicate varying levels of economic disruption, likely peaking shortly after the outbreak and gradually declining as the pandemic subsides. The data will be sourced from reputable public financial websites or institutions and ideally obtained in structured formats such as CSV, JSON, or SQL for easy parsing and analysis. Observations should be time-ordered and carefully cleaned to ensure data quality, including checking for missing values, detecting and handling outliers, standardizing units and ranges, and identifying underlying patterns (e.g., linear, polynomial, exponential, or logarithmic trends) that may inform subsequent modeling.\n",
    "\n",
