   "source": [
    "### Bitcoin Daily Closing Prices\n",
    "\n",
    "This dataset contains daily closing prices of Bitcoin (BTC), one of the most widely traded cryptocurrencies. The primary metric in this dataset is:\n",
    "- Closing Price (`Close`): The final trading price of Bitcoin on a given day, measured in USD. This value reflects the market consensus on Bitcoin's worth at the end of a trading day. Unlike traditional stock markets, cryptocurrency markets are open 24/7, so \"daily close\" usually refers to the price at 00:00 UTC or another standardized cutoff time.\n",
    "\n",
    "Other columns that appear in the dataset include:\n",
    "- Date (`date`): The calender day corresponding to each price entry\n",
    "- Open, High, Low (`USD`): Optional columns showing the opening, highest, and lowest price for the day; reflecting Bitcoin's daily volitility\n",
    "- Volume: Another optional column showing the amount, in USD, of 'volume' of Bitcoin units traded that day.\n",
    "\n",
    "Understanding this data is important for investors, analysts, and researchers interested in price trends, volatility, and correlations with other financial metrics. For instance, extreme fluctuatoins in price can indicate market instability, while trends over time can inform investor stategies and their portfolio diversification."
   ]
